  <data name="DlssNr_Advice_Restart" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Exit Magpie completely from the system tray, reopen it, then enable the effect group. Disabling and enabling the group alone cannot reset NGX. Confirm that DLSSNR shows “running”; if it fails again, copy the diagnostics for a report.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DlssNr_Advice_Files" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Open the program directory and recovery guide. Exit Magpie, restore the complete matching runtime from the package for this version, then reopen Magpie and enable the group. Confirm “DLSSNR is running”; if it still fails, copy the diagnostics.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DlssNr_Advice_Adapter" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Open the affected profile and inspect Rendering GPU. Select a compatible NVIDIA GPU only if one is available; otherwise remove DLSSNR from this effect group. Enable the group again and check its status.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DlssNr_Advice_Version" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Check the detected GPU, driver and DLL version in the details against the requirements of this version’s runtime package. Update only the component that does not meet those requirements, reopen Magpie and enable the group. If the requirements are unclear or the failure persists, copy the diagnostics.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DlssNr_Advice_Memory" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Close other GPU-intensive applications, lower the source resolution, or open this effect group and reduce DLSSNR Multi Pass to 1 if it is higher. Enable the group again and confirm “running”. If it still fails, copy the diagnostics.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DlssNr_Advice_Access" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Check the operation and path in the details. For library reads, restore readable runtime files; for NGX data writes, use a user-writable program directory. Reopen Magpie and enable the group. If no path or cause is identified, copy the diagnostics instead of changing permissions blindly.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DlssNr_Advice_Unknown" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Open the details and check the actual GPU and runtime file against this version’s package instructions. Enable the group once more and confirm “DLSSNR is running”. If it fails again, copy the diagnostics and report the failing step; temporarily remove DLSSNR to use the other effects.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DlssNr_Parameter_HdrRestricted" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This parameter is available only in the SDR DLSSNR path. HDR processing can still be running; see the status above.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Overlay_EffectParameters_Restricted" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>This parameter is not available for the current effect or processing mode, or is controlled by a paired HDR component. This is not a backend failure.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Message_DlssNrStopped" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The effect group stopped because DLSSNR failed. Open the details, follow the detected recovery steps, then enable the group again and confirm its status.</value>
  </data>
